# 100 m standoff imaging visualisation WITH uranium (the shadow case). Fires the EXACT
# production beam: physical AP9 forward-hemisphere flux, PAD- and cos-incidence-angle-
# weighted, E >= 200 MeV, 500 mrad acceptance cone, source +-400 mm. B = 0.1 G in +y.
# Central protons reaching the uranium (z = -50 m) stop/scatter (the shadow); near-axis
# ones reach the detector 100 m downstream. Most of the wide real flux leaves the
# +-0.7 m world within a few metres of the source (real ~2e-4 efficiency).
# View: side view (y-z plane), looking from +x.  Usage: MAIN.exe vis_imaging.mac
/vis/open OGL 1200x600-0+0
/vis/viewer/set/viewpointThetaPhi 90 0
/vis/viewer/set/upVector 0 0 1
/vis/viewer/set/style wireframe
/vis/viewer/set/auxiliaryEdge true
/vis/drawVolume
/vis/scene/add/trajectories rich
/vis/modeling/trajectories/create/drawByParticleID
/vis/scene/endOfEventAction accumulate
/tracking/storeTrajectory 1
/vis/viewer/flush
/run/beamOn 300
